{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T21:49:44.089Z","data":{"text":"Task 7 is complete. Both verifies pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented opt-in scenario traceability checking in lint across three new modules plus the linter call:\n\n- **`src/core/spec/traceability-lint.ts`** — `collectTraceabilityFindings` entry: builds the scenario index once from the passed import graph, reads opted-in capabilities, delta/effective scenarios, planned `## Scenarios`, ADRs, and ownership, then returns link, unreadable, and blast-radius findings. Skips all link/unreadable findings when nothing is opted in.\n- **`src/core/spec/traceability-links.ts`** — link rules: duplicate effective scenarios, added/differing-MODIFIED scenarios no scoped test names, `@scenario` tags naming missing scenarios, tagged functions with no covering test, and `@adr` tags that are missing/unaccepted/out of scope (using `sameAdrNumber` and `ownerCapabilities`). Planned scenarios count as tested and cover their tagged functions until a scoped test names them.\n- **`src/core/spec/scenario-impact.ts`** — reads each delta's altered/removed scenarios and emits the blast-radius listing and `tests.modify` warnings, with `require`-mode errors for opted-in capabilities.\n- **`src/core/spec/linter.ts`** — added `resolvedPaths` (all `resolveScope` entries, existing or not) and one `collectTraceabilityFindings` call right after impact findings, added via `addOwn`.\n- **`tests/trace-lint.test.ts`** / **`tests/trace-impact-lint.test.ts`** — 20 tests covering every listed scenario, the pricing fixture copy (intact = no finding, `tierPrice` swap = `quote: no test for \"Volume discount tiers\" covers it`), not-opted-in / nothing-opted-in equality, and direct entry assertions.\n\n`pnpm verify` passes (typechecks, build, 2034 + 88 tests, lint). Result written to `.run/results/7.md`."}}
